 },
 "notes": [
  "A turn is the history rendered with the turn's messages minus the generation prompt, minus the stop token that ends it (<|return|> after an answer, <|call|> after a call), which the stop decoder hides from the parser.",
  "The template writes a call's recipient in the header's role section (`<|start|>assistant to=functions.NAME<|channel|>commentary json<|message|>`) and each call as a message of its own, so a turn of two calls holds the first's <|call|> as text; a live stream stops at the first.",
  "The template renders the thought of a message with calls only while no later message answers; an answer's thought is dropped from the history, so a thought stands in a fixture only where the turn is the last one rendered.",
  "The tail is the prompt from its last user message; the replay starts after the prompt's last <|start|>assistant."
 ],
